  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Assessing Project Scope**\n\nOkay, I\'m starting with a skill check as per instructions. The user desires a full automated PCB trace router project, drawing from a document detailing a grid-based autorouter using Lee\'s algorithm, A* search, and conflict resolution via rip-up-and-reroute. I\'m focusing on scope now to make sure I have all the knowledge.\n\n\n**Defining Core Features**\n\nI\'ve zeroed in on the core features gleaned from the project specification. I am mapping the necessary functions, like a customizable board editor handling grid sizes, layers, and obstacle density. I also consider the application\'s underlying architecture, and the implementation of Lee\'s algorithm, A* search, and rip-up-and-reroute techniques.\n\n\n**Detailing Routing Algorithms**\n\nNow, I\'m diving deeper into the routing console and algorithmic components. I am developing specifications for Lee\'s algorithm, specifically the flood fill\'s FIFO queue and the cost/parent maps. For A* search, I am considering the use of a min-heap to optimize node selection based on the f-cost. I\'m also planning the rip-up-and-reroute process, with a focus on conflict resolution and the iterative approach.\n\n\n**Adding Visualization Capabilities**\n\nI\'m now integrating visualization as a key feature. I\'m planning step-by-step playback or instant mode for each algorithm to highlight wavefront expansion. Also, I\'m making a comparison dashboard to directly compare the outputs of all three algorithms, measuring various performance indicators. I am also working on export options like JSON and .kicad_pcb snippets.\n\n**Building Server API**\n\nI\'m developing a full-stack, Express backend API. I will have health checks, board submission endpoints, and endpoints to manage board data. I am working on the initial structure with endpoints for health checks, creating boards, and fetching them. I\'m focusing on providing the backend infrastructure to support the core routing functionality and visualizations.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 4
      nanos: 525596353
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
