  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Constructing React Components**\n\nI\'m now diving into the React component structure. I\'m focusing on creating clean, modular components for the frontend. First up is `src/components/Navbar.tsx`, the application bar, where I\'m designing the logo, title (\"Automated PCB Trace Router\"), and subtitle (\"A Grid-Based Autorouter using Lee\").\n\n\n**Designing UI Components**\n\nI\'ve got the UI component design taking shape. Right now I\'m working on the `GridCanvas.tsx` component. It\'s an interactive SVG/Canvas grid, with grid cells, layer indicators, obstacles, source/target pins with net badges, and copper traces. I\'m focusing on high performance rendering, animated wavefront highlighting, and a congestion heatmap overlay. I\'ll include click-to-place obstacles, and Vias too.\n\n\n**Developing Editor Functionality**\n\nI\'m now implementing the `BoardEditor.tsx` component, including controls for grid size, layers, and obstacle density. Tool selection is next: obstacle editing, net pin placement with auto-generated net names and colors, and clear/generate board options. I\'m also working on the netlist table and preset toolbar buttons for the board editor.\n\n\n**Analyzing Algorithm Performance**\n\nI\'m now deep-diving into the comparison dashboard. I\'ve got key metric cards displaying speedup, explored cells reduction, wirelength overhead, and rip-up convergence. Interactive Recharts charts for cell exploration, wirelength/vias, and execution time are also under development. I\'m focusing on a per-net breakdown table with status, path length, vias, and explored cells, alongside a rip-up conflict cluster graph. I\'m also planning to incorporate an algorithm info modal.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 11
      nanos: 304491175
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
