  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Verifying Server Health**\n\nI\'m currently checking the dev server\'s status and endpoint functionality. I\'m considering a quick test call to the local health endpoint. I may also implement a synchronous check or look into linting and compiling as an additional test.\n\n\n**Reviewing Project Specs**\n\nNow I\'m diving back into the project PDF. I\'m taking a fresh look at the core algorithms and data structures, specifically Lee\'s Algorithm, A* Search, and Rip-Up-and-Reroute, ensuring my mental model aligns with the requirements. It\'s also critical to re-verify the REST API endpoints.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I have completed the full implementation of the **Automated PCB Trace Router** application based on the project specification:\n\n### **Key Accomplishments & Features**\n\n1. **Routing Algorithms Core Engine**:\n   - **Lee\'s Algorithm**: Uninformed breadth-first flood fill outward from the source using a FIFO queue, cost map, and parent pointer map with early target termination.\n   - **A\\* Search**: Informed best-first search using a min-heap priority queue ordered by $f = g + h$, featuring an admissible Manhattan distance heuristic and a direction-change tie-breaker to prefer straight traces.\n   - **Rip-Up-and-Reroute**: Iterative conflict resolution controller that routes nets shortest-first, scans bounding boxes for blocking nets upon collision, rips up conflicting traces, increases per-cell traversal penalties, and clusters mutually conflicting nets using a **Disjoint-Set Union-Find** data structure with path compression and rank.\n\n2. **Express REST API Backend (`server.ts`)**:\n   - `GET /api/v1/health` \342\200\224 Service liveness and state metrics.\n   - `POST /api/v1/boards` \342\200\224 Validate and store board configurations.\n   - `GET /api/v1/boards/:id` \342\200\224 Retrieve stored boards.\n   - `POST /api/v1/boards/:id/route/lee` \342\200\224 Execute Lee\'s BFS routing.\n   - `POST /api/v1/boards/:id/route/astar` \342\200\224 Execute A* Search routing.\n   - `POST /api/v1/boards/:id/route/ripup` \342\200\224 Execute Rip-Up-and-Reroute multi-net routing.\n   - `POST /api/v1/boards/:id/compare` \342\200\224 Execute comparative benchmark across all 3 algorithms on identical input.\n   - `POST /api/v1/generate/random` & `POST /api/v1/generate/congestion` \342\200\224 Evaluation board generators.\n\n3. **Interactive Visual User Interfaces**:\n   - **Board Editor**: Customizable grid dimensions ($10 \\times 10$ to $50 \\times 50$), 1-layer or 2-layer copper modes, obstacle density controls, clickable cell painter (obstacles, source/target pins), and benchmark evaluation board presets.\n   - **Routing Console & Search Wavefront Animator**: Live SVG grid canvas rendering trace paths, via pads, pin labels, and step-by-step search wavefront expansion playback with play/pause/step controls and speed multipliers.\n   - **Benchmark Comparison Dashboard**: Metrics highlighting A* speedup ratios over Lee\'s, wirelength overhead comparisons, and interactive Recharts bar charts for cells explored, wirelengths, vias, and execution runtimes.\n   - **KiCad Exporter & Theory Guide**: Exporter generating valid `.kicad_pcb` board files or JSON configurations, along with an interactive modal detailing the computer science theory and time complexities ($O(R \\times C \\times L)$, $O(\\alpha(N))$)."
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 1
      nanos: 765047616
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
